<main>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">Gesttalt scaffold</span>
      <div class="vision">
        <h1>Federated publications, started with a clean Phoenix baseline.</h1>
        <p>
          This repository is now set up as an Elixir and Phoenix application with `mise`
          managing the toolchain. It intentionally skips Tailwind so we can keep the first commit
          focused on the application skeleton and protocol architecture.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://hexdocs.pm/phoenix/overview.html">
          Phoenix guides
        </a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://hexdocs.pm/elixir/introduction.html">
          Elixir guides
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="meta">
        <div class="card">
          <strong>Framework</strong> Phoenix {List.to_string(Application.spec(:phoenix, :vsn))}
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <strong>Toolchain</strong> Elixir and Erlang pinned in `mise.toml`
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <strong>Frontend</strong> Plain CSS bundled through esbuild, no Tailwind
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid columns-3">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>What's in place</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Phoenix application scaffolded at the repository root</li>
          <li>Postgres-ready Ecto configuration</li>
          <li>LiveView, esbuild, and the default Phoenix dev workflow</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3>What comes next</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Publication and issue/article domain models</li>
          <li>ActivityPub, WebFinger, and NodeInfo discovery endpoints</li>
          <li>IndieWeb capabilities like Micropub and Webmention</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3>Useful commands</h3>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>mise install
mise tasks run setup
mise exec -- mix setup
mise exec -- mix phx.server</code></pre>
      </article>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>
